{"title":"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Official_MAA)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Official MAA)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Same_idea,_easier_to_see)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Same idea, easier to see)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define a sequence recursively by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/4761309dc43d5e169b1dfb8851344d67b4f09192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_1(x)=|x-1|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/018ce6ca8591ad265fe3ed3b9d263372090d2751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n(x)=f_{n-1}(|x-n|)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" /> for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. Find the least value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that the sum of the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc19ca9685e2dcc4316b6dda7d448dad7254d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4a8a43081bca50199529ac2a4515c1400b0403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Official_MAA.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Official_MAA)\">Solution 1 (Official MAA)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Official MAA)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First it will be shown by induction that the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc19ca9685e2dcc4316b6dda7d448dad7254d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> are the integers\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e868cf171de048dbe138a8e176699288a16fb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, {a+2,} {a+4,} \\dots, {a + n(n-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/2972e2d79369db61da9bc64e05bd5ef2988f8a71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = n - \\frac{n(n-1)}2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>This is certainly true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that it is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f870655e74f187b4a24d371812c7665f9411ee91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = m-1 \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"14\" />, and note that the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d787f167104b85f7c5a2b7b1e8301f9bb769b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> are the solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edc26523a480377963be83881c900ef8bbbe2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x - m| = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a nonnegative zero of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9705eaadcfe2db36340a0e04aa45b3575f7c1f18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" />. Because the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9705eaadcfe2db36340a0e04aa45b3575f7c1f18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> form an arithmetic sequence with common difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> so do the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d787f167104b85f7c5a2b7b1e8301f9bb769b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" />. The greatest zero of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9705eaadcfe2db36340a0e04aa45b3575f7c1f18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> is<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cad08b7c2122b11ce7754637c000c6c9addca778.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m-1+\\frac{(m-1)(m-2)}2 =\\frac{m(m-1)}2,\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"38\" />so the greatest zero of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d787f167104b85f7c5a2b7b1e8301f9bb769b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/5/9b5bdc08bdeb789d02d4a29025adc06f4aedf368.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+\\frac{m(m-1)}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" /> and the least is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf790a632e8328a5bf03a797774f762a5d8c0bf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-\\frac{m(m-1)}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that the number of zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc19ca9685e2dcc4316b6dda7d448dad7254d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/343ce3c9376f7672390120331c8cbc2d51cd5832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n-1)}2+1=\\frac{n^2-n+2}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"212\" height=\"39\" />, and their average value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. The sum of the zeros of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc19ca9685e2dcc4316b6dda7d448dad7254d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> is<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f4320975385f08b84da88660cb0b7be881864281.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n^3-n^2+2n}2.\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"39\" />Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2f5c0388abea85e903f837e27e2616d83c72ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)=n^3-n^2+2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />, so the sum of the zeros exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1ebb3c3f4f0db6331bbb43e4f7b1bc6004ffd463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500{,}000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cef8a1c674f992e395aae86761b213c1217e333a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) &gt; 1{,}000{,}000 = 100^3\\!.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"19\" /> Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is increasing for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097569af11a8c230c95e6550101ff0b0e7ac7958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/2/fd28f0d14fe27cbfdbeb5979cb00055eeff70505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(100) = 1{,}000{,}000 - 10{,}000 + 200 = 990{,}200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948df970b7f9cb16d984f12d4ed654c72f4afba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(101)=1{,}030{,}301 - 10{,}201 + 202 = 1{,}020{,}302$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"371\" height=\"18\" /> show that the requested value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8c11da3f022ba0122f819648db790423123230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Same_idea.2C_easier_to_see.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Same_idea,_easier_to_see)\">Solution 2 (Same idea, easier to see)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Same idea, easier to see)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Starting from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/4761309dc43d5e169b1dfb8851344d67b4f09192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_1(x)=|x-1|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, we can track the solutions, the number of solutions, and their sum: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efab29c9ecd8fdf3d4f4a3444dd7a90efb18edcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c} n&amp;Solutions&amp;number&amp;sum\\\\  1&amp;1&amp;1&amp;1\\\\   2&amp;1,3&amp;2&amp;4\\\\    3&amp;0,2,4,6&amp;4&amp;12\\\\ 4&amp;-2,0,2...10&amp;7&amp;28\\\\ 5&amp;-5,-3,-1...15&amp;11&amp;55\\\\ \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"119\" />\n</p><p>It is clear that the solutions form arithmetic sequences with a difference of 2, and the negative solutions cancel out all but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad2209f276f209c8084b4f9f2c0b5cee98f64ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"40\" /> solutions. Thus, the sum of the solutions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45c24ee2dcb2d43e1c9dc03ec3dff87b9d17a6b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot [1+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"40\" />, which is a cubic function.\n(Side Note: Gergor-Newton Interpolation Formula is applicable here)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a2a8f22ef30e0f722f08e6b8a5c2ad4350c9b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot [1+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}]&gt;500,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"225\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/814ce0431ef44d3a4ba28db03ef1c46db50cfdb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot [2+n(n-1)]&gt;1,000,000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>1 million is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/6/d76aad15fc625fac6bf737bf48179875b33b1ee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^6=100^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, so the solution should be close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>100 is slightly too small, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8c11da3f022ba0122f819648db790423123230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> works. \n</p><p>~ dragnin\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/g13o0wgj4p0\">https://youtu.be/g13o0wgj4p0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II\" title=\"2020 AIME II\">2020 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2020 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002729\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 321/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8989/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.147      1 -total\n 59.05%    7.764      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.34%    5.172      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18846:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002729 and revision id 239731. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}